You are working on the Zabotik loyalty-bot project.

Read `docs/telegram-mini-app-storefront.md` before implementing Mini App tasks.

Important rules:
- Do not remove existing Telegram bot catalog.
- Keep bot catalog as fallback.
- Main ecommerce UX should be Telegram Mini App.
- Do not implement payments, fiscal receipts, delivery provider integrations, 1C, SDEK or marketplace logic.
- Do not expose admin APIs to storefront.
- Do not expose supplierPrice in storefront API.
- Do not expose hidden products.
- Do not expose unapproved image candidates.
- Do not expose bot token or API keys to frontend.
- Storefront must show only active=true and visible=true products.
- Storefront must show only approved product images.
- Order creation must validate product/shop/visibility/stock on backend.
- Do not trust frontend prices.
- Telegram initData must be validated on backend before trusting Telegram user id.
- Existing admin panel and orders page must continue working.
- Backend and frontend builds must pass.